00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.156
And AgentCore Gateway and Agent registry allows us to do just that.

00:10:00.156 --> 00:10:06.756
And hence, it's a best practice to create a published
repository of tools and agents which can be discovered.

00:10:08.196 --> 00:10:10.396
The fourth best practice is around memory.

00:10:10.556 --> 00:10:13.476
So there are two types of memory as we saw in the last session.

00:10:13.476 --> 00:10:15.756
There's a short term memory. There's a long term memory.

00:10:15.756 --> 00:10:23.316
Short term is raw conversation. Long term is basically
what insights can be culled out from that conversation.

00:10:23.316 --> 00:10:30.956
And AgentCore is able to, you know, extract preferences
and semantic facts out of the short term conversation.

00:10:31.636 --> 00:10:32.036
Now.

00:10:34.476 --> 00:10:35.676
Now suppose you.

00:10:36.716 --> 00:10:39.556
So let's take an example. So. So if there is an agent.

00:10:39.636 --> 00:10:44.916
If there is a user who's interacting with an agent
and multiple agents in the enterprise,

00:10:46.116 --> 00:10:49.556
the. The user builds a persona. Persona of preferences.

00:10:49.556 --> 00:10:56.916
Persona of way of doing things which can then become a profile
and it can automatically be extracted out by memory.

00:10:56.916 --> 00:10:58.316
So let's take an example.

00:10:59.716 --> 00:11:01.956
This is a travel agent and I ask it a question.

00:11:01.956 --> 00:11:04.276
Please plan a vacation for me and my family.

00:11:04.756 --> 00:11:10.196
And you know, the agent doesn't know anything about me,
doesn't know what kind of vacation I like, where am I based,

00:11:10.196 --> 00:11:17.996
who's in my family? So it's asking me a bunch of questions now based
on my previous conversations with this agent

00:11:17.996 --> 00:11:20.716
and with other agents in the organization.

00:11:21.236 --> 00:11:27.276
AgentCore Memory can actually extract all these preferences
out and then make it seamlessly available to all the agents.

00:11:27.836 --> 00:11:33.076
So, so suppose you know these these semantic
facts have been culled out already, right?

00:11:33.116 --> 00:11:39.076
So it knows what kind of vacation do I like,
who's in my family, what kind of budget and all of those things.

00:11:39.076 --> 00:11:45.476
And now if this is provided to the agent,
then the response is a lot very different.

00:11:45.476 --> 00:11:53.596
It is much more relevant. It is much more personalized, and the whole
interaction becomes very, you know, productive and efficient.

00:11:56.716 --> 00:11:57.276
Right.

00:11:58.196 --> 00:12:00.876
The fifth best practice is around observability.

00:12:01.356 --> 00:12:04.996
Now, Agentic AI apps are complicated, right?

00:12:05.036 --> 00:12:09.836
Because what they do is not actually written
in code, which you can review.

00:12:09.956 --> 00:12:13.236
It's based on reasoning of reasoning of LLMs.

00:12:13.756 --> 00:12:16.876
And so suppose you have to figure out if something goes wrong.

00:12:16.876 --> 00:12:24.436
How do you troubleshoot. Or suppose you have to, you know, prove
to an A in a compliance audit that the agent followed the guideline.

00:12:24.436 --> 00:12:27.836
How do you do that? So the answer here is observability, right.

00:12:27.876 --> 00:12:31.556
And AgentCore Observability is open telemetry compliant.

00:12:32.076 --> 00:12:37.196
So let's take an example. This is a multi-agent
application where, you know, I give an objective.

00:12:37.236 --> 00:12:39.556
We talked about an objective. We give an objective.

00:12:39.556 --> 00:12:42.876
Figure out the best vacation for a family of certain size

00:12:42.876 --> 00:12:47.916
in a certain part of the world under the constraints
of some amount of days and a budget.

00:12:47.916 --> 00:12:52.476
And this objective is given to three agents,
all powered by different models.

00:12:52.876 --> 00:12:53.396
And,

00:12:54.756 --> 00:12:58.636
and, you know, they can do their independent research,
come back with a recommendation.

00:12:58.636 --> 00:13:02.716
And then there is a fourth agent
which will drive consensus between them.

00:13:02.716 --> 00:13:07.716
So as this app is running, you can see,
you know, a lot of events are being generated.

00:13:08.036 --> 00:13:13.396
And finally, you know, the, the agents will come back
with the recommendation, there will be consensus.

00:13:13.396 --> 00:13:19.996
And finally they will come back with a,
with a recommendation that, okay, you should now go to, you know,

00:13:20.036 --> 00:13:22.836
you know, that's the recommendation across.

00:13:22.876 --> 00:13:26.476
And those are the citations which support that recommendation.

00:13:26.716 --> 00:13:34.796
But suppose you have to deep dive and figure out what were
those three disputed points and why were they not selected.

00:13:35.196 --> 00:13:38.516
Right. And suppose that has to be done then how do you do that again?

00:13:38.516 --> 00:13:42.796
The answer is observability.
So we have captured all these events in Langfuse.

00:13:42.796 --> 00:13:47.076
Langfuse is an observability tool which supports open telemetry.

00:13:47.396 --> 00:13:50.036
And we'll deep dive into one of those four agents here.

00:13:50.036 --> 00:13:58.036
So what you can see here is the complete event loop of the agent
is visible based on the traces which were captured, which tools,

00:13:58.036 --> 00:14:00.516
how many times it was called, what were the inputs,

00:14:00.516 --> 00:14:05.316
what were the outputs and what decisions the agent
took in that whole event loop is visible.

00:14:05.316 --> 00:14:07.676
So now if you have to troubleshoot, you can do it.

00:14:07.676 --> 00:14:12.036
If you have to, you know, use this information for a compliance audit.

00:14:12.036 --> 00:14:16.076
You can do it. And you want to explain
why an agent did something, you can do it.

00:14:16.076 --> 00:14:20.476
Hence observability is absolutely non-negotiable
in any Agentic application.

00:14:22.396 --> 00:14:27.276
Lastly, but again, not the least, everybody has the same,

00:14:28.396 --> 00:14:32.356
you know, model. Everybody has access to the same frameworks.

00:14:33.276 --> 00:14:38.676
What differentiates you is the data you have and what
you do with your data and these models, right?

00:14:38.716 --> 00:14:46.356
Hence, it's very critical to create a data foundation
which can power your Agentic AI solutions.

